{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bin Smoothing.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bin Smoothing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bin smoothing bin smoothing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bin Smoothing.md","fileName":"Bin Smoothing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bin Smoothing","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 20:21\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Statistical Learning and Validation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Statistical Learning and Validation","LOESS","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bin Smoothing.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bin Smoothing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bin smoothing bin smoothing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bin Smoothing.md","fileName":"Bin Smoothing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bin Smoothing","heading":"Bin Smoothing","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Bin smoothing estimates an unknown relationship by grouping nearby predictor values and averaging their outcomes. It assumes the conditional expectation changes little within a sufficiently small neighborhood, so a constant can approximate each local segment.\n\nNarrow bins follow local variation but contain fewer observations and produce noisy estimates; wider bins stabilize averages but can erase curvature. [[LOESS]] replaces each local constant with a more flexible local polynomial.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Statistical Learning and Validation","LOESS","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bin Smoothing.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bin Smoothing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bin smoothing bin smoothing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bin Smoothing.md","fileName"